    3) 
"Why is S3 secure?"
    "S3 provides multiple layers of security. We can control access using IAM policies
    and bucket policies, prevent accidental public exposure using Block Public Access, encrypt data at rest using SSE-S3 or SSE-KMS and data in transit using HTTPS. We can also enable versioning and Object Lock to protect data from accidental deletion or modification, while CloudTrail provides auditing of API activity. So S3 security follows a defense-in-depth approach."
1) Public access Enable
2) ACL Enable  (At bucket Level)
3) ACL need to enable object Level
access can be provide to the object 

policies will be written in the form of json format
